  "title": "67: Al-Mulk الملك",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ بِيَدِهِ الْمُلْكُ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرُۙ‏(1)\nTABAARAKAL LAZEE BEYADEHIL MULK, WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERO.\nHallowed is He in Whose hand is the kingdom (of the heaven and the earth), and He, over all things is All-Powerful\nاۨلَّذِىْ خَلَقَ الْمَوْتَ وَالْحَيٰوةَ لِيَبْلُوَكُمْ اَيُّكُمْ اَحْسَنُ عَمَلًاؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْغَفُوْرُۙ‏(2)\nNIL LAZEE KHALAQAL MAWTA WAL HAYAATA LE-YABLOWAKUM AYYOKUM AHSANO A’MALAA, WA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL GHAFOORUL.\nWho created death and life that he may try you (to prove) which of you is best in deeds; He is the Ever-Prevalent, the Oft-Forgiving\nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمٰوٰتٍ طِبَاقًا ؕ مَا تَرٰى فِىْ خَلْقِ الرَّحْمٰنِ مِنْ تَفٰوُتٍ ؕ فَارْجِعِ الْبَصَرَۙ هَلْ تَرٰى مِنْ فُطُوْرٍ‏(3)\nLAZEE KHALAQA SAB-A’ SAMAAWAATIN TEBAAQAA, MAA TARAA FEE KHALQIR RAHMAANE MIN TAFAAWOT, FAR-JE-I’L BASARA, HAL TARAA MIN FOTOOR.\nWho created the seven heavens layer above layer: thou seest not in the creation of the Beneficent (God) any defect or incongruity. Then look thou again; Seest thou any gap?\nثُمَّ ارْجِعِ الْبَصَرَ كَرَّتَيْنِ يَنْقَلِبْ اِلَيْكَ الْبَصَرُ خَاسِئًا وَّهُوَ حَسِيْرٌ‏(4)\nSUMMAR JE-I’L BASARA KARRATAYNE YANQALIB ELAYKAL BASARO KHAA-SE-ANW WA HOWA HASEER.\nThen repeat thou (thy) gaze again and again, thy gaze shall return unto thee dulled, being Wearied\nوَلَقَدْ زَيَّنَّا السَّمَآءَ الدُّنْيَا بِمَصَابِيْحَ وَجَعَلْنٰهَا رُجُوْمًا لِّلشَّيٰطِيْنِ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لَهُمْ عَذَابَ السَّعِيْرِ‏(5)\nWA LAQAD ZAYYANNAS SAMAAA-AD DUNYAA BE MASAABEEHA WA JA-A’LNAAHAA ROJOOMAL LISH-SHAYAATEENE WA A-A’TADNAA LAHUM A’ZAABAS SA-E’ER.\nIndeed, have We adorned the lower heaven nearest to the world with lamps (i.e., the stars), and We have made them (as) missiles to repulse away the Satans, and We have prepared for them the chastisement of the flaming fire\nوَلِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْ عَذَابُ جَهَنَّمَؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(6)\nWA LIL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-RABBEHIM A’ZAABO JAHANNAM, WA BE’SAL MASEER.\nAnd for those who disbelieve in their Lord is the chastisement of the hell, and evil is the destination\nاِذَاۤ اُلْقُوْا فِيْهَا سَمِعُوْا لَهَا شَهِيْقًا وَّهِىَ تَفُوْرُۙ‏(7)\nEZAA ULQOO FEEHAA SAMEO’O LAHAA SHA-HEEQANW WA HEYA TAFOORO.\nWhen they shall be flung into it, they shall hear its roaring as it boileth up\nتَكَادُ تَمَيَّزُ مِنَ الْغَيْظِؕ كُلَّمَاۤ اُلْقِىَ فِيْهَا فَوْجٌ سَاَلَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَاۤ اَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ نَذِيْرٌ‏(8)\nTAKAADO TAMAYYAZO MENAL GHAYZ, KULLAMAA ULQEYA FEEHAA FAWJUN SA-ALAHUM KHAZANATOHAA ALAM YAATEKUM NAZEER.\nAs it would burst with rage; Whenever a group is flung into it, its keepers shall ask them; “Came not there unto you a warner?\nقَالُوْا بَلٰى قَدْ جَآءَنَا نَذِيْرٌ ۙ فَكَذَّبْنَا وَقُلْنَا مَا نَزَّلَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ ۖۚ اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ كَبِيْرٍ‏(9)\nQAALOO BALAA QAD JAAA-ANAA NAZEERUN, FA-KAZZABNAA WA QULNAA MAA NAZZALAL LAAHO MIN SHAY, IN ANTUM ILLAA FEE ZALAALIN KABEER.\nThey shall say: “Yea! Indeed, a warner did come unto us, but we belied (him) and said we: “God hath sent not down aught, ye are in naught but a vast delusion!\nوَقَالُوْا لَوْ كُنَّا نَسْمَعُ اَوْ نَعْقِلُ مَا كُنَّا فِىْۤ اَصْحٰبِ السَّعِيْرِ‏(10)\nWA QAALOO LAW KUNNAA NASMA-O AW NA’QELO MAA KUNNA FEE ASHAABIS SA-E’ER.\nAnd they shall say: “Had we but hearkened (unto them) or pondered (over what they said), we would not have been amidst the fellows in the flaming fire\nفَاعْتَرَفُوْا بِذَنْۢبِهِمْۚ فَسُحْقًا لِّاَصْحٰبِ السَّعِيْرِ‏(11)\nFA’TARAFOO BE-ZAMBEHIM, FA-SOHQAL LE-ASHAABIS SA-E’ER.\nSo shall they confess their sins, but far will be (from mercy) the fellows in blazing fire\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَيْبِ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(12)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM BIL-GHAYBE LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN KABEER.\nVerily, those who fear their Lord in secret, for them shall be forgiveness and a great recompense\nوَاَسِرُّوْا قَوْلَكُمْ اَوِ اجْهَرُوْا بِهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(13)\nWA ASIRROO QAWLAKUM AWIJ-HAROO BEH, INNAHU A’LEEMUM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nAnd conceal ye your word or declare it; Verily, He is the Knower of whatsoever is in the breasts (hearts)\nاَلَا يَعْلَمُ مَنْ خَلَقَؕ وَهُوَ اللَّطِيْفُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(14)\nALAA YA’LAMO MAN KHALAQ, WA HOWAL LATEEFUL KHABEER.\nWhat! Knoweth not He that created? and He is the Subtle, the All-Aware\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ ذَلُوْلًا فَامْشُوْا فِىْ مَنَاكِبِهَا وَكُلُوْا مِنْ رِّزْقِهٖؕ وَاِلَيْهِ النُّشُوْرُ‏(15)\nHOWAL LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA ZALOOLAN FAM-SHOO FEE MANAAKEBEHAA WA KOLOO MIR RIZQEH, WA ELAYHIN NOSHOOR.\nHe it is Who made for you the earth subservient, traVerse ye then its broad sides, and eat ye of His provision; and unto Him (alone) is the return\nءَاَمِنْتُمْ مَّنْ فِىْ السَّمَآءِ اَنْ يَّخْسِفَ بِكُمُ الْاَرْضَ فَاِذَا هِىَ تَمُوْرُۙ‏(16)\nA-AMINTUM MAN FIS SAMAAA-E ANY YAKHSEFA BEKOMUL ARZA FA-EZAA HEYA TAMOORO.\nWhat! deem ye yourself secure of He Who (ruleth) in the heaven (as well), that He will cause not the earth to swallow you up? Then lo! it shall quake\nاَمْ اَمِنْتُمْ مَّنْ فِى السَّمَآءِ اَنْ يُّرْسِلَ عَلَيْكُمْ حَاصِبًا ؕ فَسَتَعْلَمُوْنَ كَيْفَ نَذِيْرِ‏(17)\nAM AMINTUM MAN FIS SAMAAA-E ANY YURSELA A’LAYKUM HAASEBAA, FA-SA-TA’LAMOONA KAYFA NAZEER.\nOr deem ye yourself secure of He Who (ruleth) in the heaven (as well), will send not down upon you a stone-charged violent storm; Then shall ye know how (terrible) My warning is\nوَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ نَكِيْرِ‏(18)\nWA LAQAD KAZZABAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FA-KAYFA KAANA NAKEER.\nAnd indeed belied those before them (My signs): how (terrible) then was My wrath\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلَى الطَّيْرِ فَوْقَهُمْ صٰٓفّٰتٍ وَّيَقْبِضْنَؕؔ ۘ مَا يُمْسِكُهُنَّ اِلَّا الرَّحْمٰنُؕ اِنَّهٗ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(19)\nAWA LAM YARAW ELAT TAYRE FAWQAHUM SAAAF-FAATINW WA YAQBIZN, MAA YUMSEKOHUNNA ILLAR RAHMAAN, INNAHU BEKULLE SHAY-IM BASEER.\nBehold they not the birds above them, outstretching (their wings), and contracting (them)? upholdeth them not save the Beneficent (God); for verily He well seeth everything\nاَمَّنْ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ هُوَ جُنْدٌ لَّكُمْ يَنْصُرُكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ الرَّحْمٰنِؕ اِنِ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ غُرُوْرٍۚ‏(20)\nAMMAN HAAZAL LAZEE HOWA JUNDUL LAKUM YANSOROKUM MIN DOONIR RAHMAAN, ENIL KAAFEROONA ILLAA FEE GHOROOR.\nOr who is that who can be a host for you to succour you besides the Beneficent (God)? the disbelievers are but in mere delusion\nاَمَّنْ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ يَرْزُقُكُمْ اِنْ اَمْسَكَ رِزْقَهٗ ۚ بَلْ لَّجُّوْا فِىْ عُتُوٍّ وَّنُفُوْرٍ‏(21)\nAMMAN HAAZAL LAZEE YARZOQOKUM IN AMSAKA RIZQAH, BAL LAJJOO FEE O’TUWWINW WA NOFOOR.\nOr who is that who can provide you with sustenance should He withhold His sustenance? Yet persist they in disdain and aversion (against the Truth)\nاَفَمَنْ يَّمْشِىْ مُكِبًّا عَلٰى وَجْهِهٖۤ اَهْدٰٓى اَمَّنْ يَّمْشِىْ سَوِيًّا عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(22)\nAFAMANY YAMSHEE MOKIBBAN A’LAA WAJHEHI AHDAA AMMANY YAMSHEE SAWIYYAN A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nWhat! is he who goeth along grovelling on his face, better guided or he who walketh upright upon the straight path?\nقُلْ هُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَكُمْ وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَ الْاَفْئِدَةَ  ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(23)\nQUL HOWAL LAZEE AN-SHA-A LAKUM WA JA-A’LA LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WAL ABSAARA WAL AF-EDA, QALEELAM MAA TASHKOROON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “He it is Who brought you (into being) and made for you the ears and the eyes and the hearts; yet how little is it that ye thank!\nقُلْ هُوَ الَّذِىْ ذَرَاَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(24)\nQUL HOWAL LAZEE ZARA-AKUM FIL ARZE WA ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nSay thou: “He it is Who hath spread you in the earth and unto Him (alone) shall ye all be gathered\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(25)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAL WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd say they: “When shall this appointment come to pass, if ye be truthful?\nقُلْ اِنَّمَا الْعِلْمُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَاِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(26)\nQUL INNAMAL I’LMO I’NDAL LAAH, WA INNAMAA ANAA NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nSay thou: “Verily the knowledge (of it) is only with God, and verily I am only an open Warner\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْهُ زُلْفَةً سِیْٓئَتْ وُجُوْهُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَقِيْلَ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَدَّعُوْنَ‏(27)\nFALAMMAA RA-AW-HO ZULFATAN SEEE-AT WOJOOHUL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA QEELA HAAZAL LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TADDA-O’ON.\nBut when they shall see it nigh, grieved shall be the faces of those who disbelieve, and it shall be said (unto them): “This is what ye have been calling for\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ اَهْلَكَنِىَ اللّٰهُ وَمَنْ مَّعِىَ اَوْ رَحِمَنَا ۙ فَمَنْ يُّجِيْرُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ مِنْ عَذَابٍ اَلِيْمٍ‏(28)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN AHLAKANEYAL LAAHO WA MAM MA-E’YA AW RAHEMANAA, FAMANY YOJEERUL KAAFEREENA MIN A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nSay thou: “See ye? If God were to destroy me and those with me or He bestoweth mercy on us, yet who can protect the disbelievers from the painful chastisement?\nقُلْ هُوَ الرَّحْمٰنُ اٰمَنَّا بِهٖ وَعَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْنَاۚ فَسَتَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ هُوَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(29)\nQUL HOWAR RAHMAANO AAMANNAA BEHI WA A’LAYHE TAWAKKALNAA, FA-SATA’LAMOONA MAN HOWA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nSay thou: “He is the Beneficent (God)! believe we in Him and on Him (alone) do we rely; so ye shall come to know who it is that is in manifest straying\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ اَصْبَحَ مَآؤُكُمْ غَوْرًا فَمَنْ يَّاْتِيْكُمْ بِمَآءٍ مَّعِيْنٍ‏(30)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN ASBAHA MAAA-OKUM GHAWRAN FAMANY YA’TEEKUM BE-MAAA-IM MA-E’EN.\nSay thou: “See ye? if your water should go down (into the earth), who then can bring you flowing water?",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 30 verses. It is also called Munjiyah because it saves the one who recites it from the torment of the grave. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) likened the recitation of this Surah to the staying awake on the night of Qadr. He (s.a.w.a.) also wished that every believer would memorize this Surah and know it by heart. He said that this Surah will remove its reciter from Hellfire and take him to Jannah.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) said that reciting this Surah at night keeps one under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) until morning. Recitation on the night of Eid gives the reward of staying awake the whole night in worship. If recited on a person who has just died, his soul gets immediate relief. Memorizing this Surah has great reward. If memorized, this Surah acts as a protection from the torment of the grave, and it intercedes on behalf of the one who has memorized it on the Day of Judgement."
